@prefix : <#> .
@prefix schema: <http://schema.org/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix onto: <../ontology.ttl#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .

<> a schema:CreativeWork ;
    schema:name "Resolver-Pattern Hyperlinks for Referenced Posts"@en ;
    schema:description "HowTo for the standing rule: whenever a response references other posts (weblog posts, articles, papers), the reference is a Markdown hyperlink through the URIBurner resolver, single-encoded, with each resolver URL verified (HTTP 200) before use. Companion to preferences.ttl Step 200."@en ;
    schema:dateCreated "2026-08-14T22:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:dateModified "2026-08-14T22:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    schema:author <https://www.linkedin.com/in/kidehen#this> ;
    schema:about :hyperlinkingReferencedPosts .

:hyperlinkingReferencedPosts a schema:HowTo ;
    schema:name "Hyperlinking Referenced Posts via the Resolver"@en ;
    schema:description "Procedure for turning a reference to another post into a verified, resolver-pattern hyperlink in a response."@en ;
    schema:step :step1, :step2, :step3, :step4 .

:step1 a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 1 ;
    schema:name "Take the post's clean IRI — never a pre-encoded string"@en ;
    schema:text """Start from the post's actual IRI with literal characters (apostrophes, spaces, brackets) — e.g.:

  http://www.openlinksw.com/dataspace/kidehen@openlinksw.com/weblog/kidehen@openlinksw.com's BLOG [127]/231

Never feed a pre-encoded URL (one already containing %27, %20, %5B) into the encoder: quoting it again produces %2527/%2520 double-encoding, which the resolver-double-encoding gate rejects."""@en .

:step2 a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 2 ;
    schema:name "Compute the resolver URL with a tool (single encoding)"@en ;
    schema:text """Resolver pattern:

  https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url={url-encoded-iri}

Compute the percent-encoding programmatically (e.g. urllib.parse.quote(iri, safe='')). One url-decode pass on the query value must yield the clean post IRI — if it yields another describe/?url= or still-encoded text, it is double-wrapped."""@en .

:step3 a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 3 ;
    schema:name "Verify each resolver URL resolves (HTTP 200) before use"@en ;
    schema:text """curl -s -L -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' 'https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url={encoded}'

Only include the hyperlink if the resolver returns HTTP 200. A resolver URL that 404s or times out is worse than no link — drop it or ask the user for the correct URL. Never fabricate the encoding by hand."""@en .

:step4 a schema:HowToStep ;
    schema:position 4 ;
    schema:name "Render every referenced post as a resolver hyperlink"@en ;
    schema:text """In the response, wrap the post title (or a descriptive label) as a Markdown hyperlink to the verified resolver URL:

  [Do We Need the Semantic Web?](https://linkeddata.uriburner.com/describe/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.openlinksw.com%2Fdataspace%2Fkidehen%40openlinksw.com%2Fweblog%2Fkidehen%40openlinksw.com%27s%20BLOG%20%5B127%5D%2F231)

Never emit a bare post URL and never link directly to the source site — the resolver is the canonical hyperlink surface. Local file references (session memory, artifacts) keep their local relative paths."""@en .
